<title>USA: Mattel Q1 net shr hits loss after merger.</title>
<headline>Mattel Q1 net shr hits loss after merger.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>MATTEL, INC. AND SUBSIDIARIES</p>
<p>CONSOLIDATED STATEMENTS OF INCOME</p>
<p>								  FOR THE</p>
<p>							 THREE MONTHS ENDED</p>
<p>							 MAR. 31,  MAR. 31,</p>
<p>(In thousands, except per share amounts)  1997 (b)  1996 (b)  Net Sales					    $693,520 $683,999</p>
<p>  Cost of sales					370,709  361,125</p>
<p> Gross Profit					  322,811  322,874</p>
<p>  Advertising and promotion expenses	   102,626  100,104</p>
<p>Other selling and administrative expenses  185,286  169,581</p>
<p>  Integration/restructuring costs (c)	  275,000	  0</p>
<p>  Other expense, net				   7,882    4,499</p>
<p> Operating Profit (Loss)			 (247,983)   48,690</p>
<p>   Interest expense				   19,636   19,893</p>
<p>  Income (Loss) Before Income Taxes	  (267,619)   28,797</p>
<p>   (Benefit) provision for income taxes     (62,995)    8,263</p>
<p> Net Income (Loss)				 (204,624)   20,534</p>
<p>	     Net Income (Loss) Per Share (a) (d) (0.72)    0.07</p>
<p>Average Number of Common and Common</p>
<p>   Equivalent Shares Outstanding (d)	   288,382  298,858</p>
<p>MATTEL, INC. AND SUBSIDIARIES, PRE-MERGER</p>
<p>CONSOLIDATED STATEMENTS OF INCOME</p>
<p>								   FOR THE</p>
<p>							 THREE MONTHS ENDED</p>
<p>							 MAR. 31,  MAR. 31,</p>
<p>(In thousands, except per share amounts)  1997 (e)  1996 (e)  Net Sales					    $568,528 $585,879</p>
<p>    Cost of sales				    293,643  300,102</p>
<p> Gross Profit					  274,885  285,777</p>
<p>   Advertising and promotion expenses	   77,888   80,289</p>
<p>Other selling and administrative expenses</p>
<p>							   156,583  142,920</p>
<p>   Other expense, net				  6,754    3,665</p>
<p> Operating Profit				     33,660   58,903</p>
<p>   Interest expense				   14,637   14,418</p>
<p> Income Before Income Taxes			 19,023   44,485</p>
<p>   Provision for income taxes			5,900   14,600</p>
<p> Net Income					     13,123   29,885</p>
<p>		 Net Income Per Share		   0.05     0.11</p>
<p>Average Number of Common and Common</p>
<p>   Equivalent Shares Outstanding		 274,644  281,836</p>
<p>NOTE: (a) Primary income per share for the quarter, before the $0.73 per share effect of the merger-related non-recurring charge of $210 million after taxes, was $0.01 per share.</p>
<p>(b) Consolidated results for all periods are restated for the merger with Tyco Toys Inc.</p>
<p>(c) Represents a non-recurring charge for transaction, integration and restructuring costs related to the Tyco merger. The related tax benefit of $65 million is included in the provision for income taxes.</p>
<p>(d) Share and per share data for all periods presented reflect the retroactive effect of shares issued pursuant to the Tyco merger.</p>
<p>(e) Consolidated results exclude Tyco and all merger-related transactions.</p>
